# VS Code Marketplace listing — do not regress

Marketplace listing content is **sourced from the VSIX**, which packs `package.json` + root `README.md`. Every publish **overwrites** the live listing. Portal-only edits are temporary and get wiped.

Publisher / item: `coop-ai.coop-ai`  
Listing: https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=coop-ai.coop-ai

## Source of truth

| Listing field | Edit here only |
|---|---|
| Short description | `package.json` → `description` |
| Categories | `package.json` → `categories` — **exactly** `["AI", "Chat"]` |
| Overview + first screenshot | Root `README.md` (opening paragraphs + first image) |
| Banner asset | `website/public/screenshots/docs/extension-from-your-stack.png` (must stay reachable at the README URL) |

## Hard fails (never ship)

| Reject | Prefer |
|---|---|
| Adding `Machine Learning` (or any third category) | `AI` first, then `Chat` only |
| Replacing the README opener with old “repo graph, Slack, and tickets” copy | Keep the three-paragraph AI / zero-clone / indexed-map opener |
| First README image pointing at `extension-sidebar-light.png` (or any non-Stack hero) | First image = Stack banner URL |
| Deleting the Stack PNG without updating README + redeploying the site | Update URL + asset together |
| Relying on Publisher Management to “remember” category/copy | Fix git, bump version, upload new VSIX |

## Before packaging / publishing

1. Run **`npm run test:marketplace-listing`** (also in `test:ci`).
2. Bump `package.json` `version` + `CHANGELOG.md` (+ `COOP_EXTENSION_BUILD_ID` when shipping a distinguishable VSIX).
3. `npm run package` → upload `coop-ai.vsix` (or `vsce publish` with a PAT).
4. Confirm site image is live before relying on the README screenshot URL.

Playbook: `docs/distribution/02-vscode-marketplace.md`.

## Self-check

Would the next VSIX put the listing back under **Machine Learning** or restore the old sidebar-first screenshot? If yes, fail.
